Design note, VP-112.

A speaker embedding never leaves this process. The enrolment pipeline builds
one embedding for every exemplar, seals it under the profile key, and writes
only the sealed form to the store. Diagnostics may record that an embedding
was computed, how long the computation took and whether it was accepted, but
never what it contained.

Reviewers should be able to follow this argument end to end without ever
reading a vector, so nothing in this note is allowed to look like one.
